deploy - Deploy the release to the target.

Usage:
  lask run deploy <target> [<files> ...] [--token <String>] --region <String> [--dry-run] [--retries <Number | Null>]

Every file under the release directory is uploaded; nothing is removed.

Parameters:
  target : String
      Where it goes.
  ...files : Array<String>
      The files, relative to the release directory.
  --token : String = <secret>
      The credential of the target.
  --region : String  (required)
  --dry-run : Bool = false
      Print what would be uploaded.
  --retries : Number | Null = null

Returns:
  String
      What was uploaded.

Environments:
  #alpine:3.22.2  registry

Examples:
  lask run deploy prod a.txt b.txt --token $TOKEN

Defined at main.lask:13

